@prefix rdf:      <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:      <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dc:       <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/> .
@prefix dcterms:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix protys:   <http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/> .

# ============================================================================
# PROTYS(KB) - Ontology Network for Semantic Interoperability in Manufacturing
# Master Ontology - Imports all modules
# ============================================================================

protys:protys-kb a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://w3id.org/protys/ontology/protys-kb/1.0> ;
    dc:title "PROTYS(KB) - Knowledge Base for Manufacturing Interoperability"@en ;
    dc:title "PROTYS(KB) - Base de Conocimiento para Interoperabilidad en Manufactura"@es ;
    dc:creator "Álvaro Fraga Moreira" ;
    dc:description """PROTYS(KB) is an ontology network designed to enable semantic
    interoperability between heterogeneous manufacturing information systems (ERP, MES,
    SCADA, LIMS). It integrates domain concepts from international standards ISO 14040
    (Life Cycle Assessment) and ISO 15531 (MANDATE - Manufacturing Data) through a
    modular architecture with SWRL-based alignment rules."""@en ;
    dc:date "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dc:rights "Academic Use - PhD Thesis, Universidad de Carabobo" ;
    dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0" ;

    # Module imports
    owl:imports protys:core ;
    owl:imports protys:product ;
    owl:imports protys:process ;
    owl:imports protys:resource ;
    owl:imports protys:enterprise ;
    owl:imports protys:iso14040 ;
    owl:imports protys:iso15531 ;
    owl:imports protys:alignment ;
    owl:imports protys:paint-ext ;

    # Annotations about the network
    rdfs:comment """
    Architecture (thesis Ch. 3, Table 3.4): 7 domain modules + 1 alignment module
    = 8 OWL ontologies, plus the case-study extension (derived ontology, Ch. 4 4.4.1).

    Core Layer (Nivel Principal):
      - core-concepts.owl     : 4 classes (Product, Process, Resource, Enterprise)

    Refinement Modules (Nivel de Refinamiento):
      - product-module.owl    : Thing, Substance, Production_Item, Product, Production_Component,
                                Product_Information, Physical_Characteristics, Instruction, Fact,
                                Concept, Customer (Fig. 3.8)
      - process-module.owl    : Natural_Process, Artificial_Process, Procedure, Process_Activity,
                                Procedure_Activity, Process_Plan, Process_Plant, Parameters (Fig. 3.7)
      - resource-module.owl   : Behaviour, Capability, Tool, Equip, Device, Material,
                                Process_Material, Product_Material, Raw_Material, Person, Role,
                                File, Resource_Related_File, Product_Related_File, Activity (Figs. 3.9-3.12)
      - enterprise-module.owl : Station, Cell, Shop, Factory, Location (Fig. 3.13)

    Standard Modules (Nivel de Estandares):
      - iso14040-module.owl   : 15 classes (Listado 3.1: LCAStudy, ElementaryFlow, UnitProcess, ...)
      - iso15531-module.owl   : 18 classes (Listado 3.2: ManufacturingResource, WorkOrder, Lot, ...)

    Alignment Layer (Capa de Alineamiento):
      - alignment-rules.owl      : 7 owl:equivalentClass axioms (Listado 3.3) + SWRL rules R01-R26
                                   (22 con cuerpo SWRL DL-safe; R07/R16/R19/R26 son patrones
                                   SPARQL ASK en alignment-queries.sparql)
      - iso10303-alignment-rules.owl : R27-R29 (extensibilidad AP242, thesis 5.4.3)

    Case-study extension (derived ontology):
      - paint-case-extension.owl : clases del caso de pinturas como subclases de los
                                   conceptos de PROTYS(KB) (BatchProcess, Formulation, ...)
    """@en .

# ============================================================================
# Named Graph Mapping (for Fuseki deployment)
# ============================================================================
# urn:protys:core        → core-concepts.owl
# urn:protys:product     → product-module.owl
# urn:protys:process     → process-module.owl
# urn:protys:resource    → resource-module.owl
# urn:protys:enterprise  → enterprise-module.owl
# urn:protys:iso14040    → iso14040-module.owl
# urn:protys:iso15531    → iso15531-module.owl
# urn:protys:alignment   → alignment-rules.owl
# urn:protys:paint-ext   → paint-case-extension.owl
# urn:protys:kb          → protys-kb.ttl (this file)
# urn:protys:instances   → paint-case-study-instances.ttl
# urn:protys:erp:adempiere → paint-instances-adempiere.ttl
# urn:protys:erp:odoo    → paint-instances-odoo.ttl
